ort VLAN switch: eth1 (link to node2) placed untagged in VLAN 10, eth2 (link to node3) placed untagged in VLAN 20, on a VLAN-filtering Linux bridge (br0) with per-VLAN SVIs (br0.10=192.168.10.1, br0.20=192.168.20.1). node2 (192.168.10.2) and node3 (192.168.20.2) each retain a working link to node1 in their own VLAN, while direct L2 reachability between node2 and node3 is blocked (verified even with an overlapping subnet to rule out mere subnet mismatch). Persisted config via a systemd oneshot service on node1 and NetworkManager profiles on node2/node3. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes, confirming boot-id changes and full post-restart recovery of VLAN segmentation, connectivity, and isolation.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Mapped node1's physical links via temporary IP/ping tests: eth1 to node2, eth2 to node3\",\"Cleaned SONiC docker0 class-E address leak on node1\",\"Built a vlan_filtering Linux bridge (br0) on node1 enslaving eth1 and eth2\",\"Set eth1 as untagged access port in VLAN 10, eth2 as untagged access port in VLAN 20, removed default VLAN 1 membership\",\"Created br0.10/br0.20 SVIs on node1 with IPs 192.168.10.1/24 and 192.168.20.1/24\",\"Assigned node2=192.168.10.2/24 and node3=192.168.20.2/24 on enp8s0 via persistent NetworkManager profiles\",\"Verified node1<->node2 and node1<->node3 connectivity within their respective VLANs\",\"Verified node2/node3 L2 isolation using an overlapping-subnet test (192.168.10.3 on node3) to rule out subnet-mismatch false negative\",\"Persisted node1's bridge/VLAN config via systemd oneshot unit vlan-access-segmentation.service, enabled at boot, verified idempotent\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and service/connectivity baseline on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node2, node3, then node1 sequentially (one at a time), polling until each returned and confirming boot_id changed\",\"Re-verified post-restart on node1: SONiC docker containers (swss/bgp/syncd/database) healthy, VLAN bridge config auto-restored by systemd unit\",\"Re-verified post-restart connectivity node1<->node2, node1<->node3, and node2/node3 isolation all still hold\",\"Cleaned up all temporary test IP addresses used for isolation testing\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Identify which node1 interface connects to which host\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2c8bec45d1054c59\",\"cmd-faaefc22c63a485d\"],\"summary\":\"Temporary IP assignment and directional ping test proved eth1 reaches node2 (172.31.99.2) and eth2 reaches node3 (172.31.98.3)\"},{\"requirement\":\"eth1/eth2 configured as untagged access ports in separate VLANs on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ab32dc98bf954962\",\"cmd-97e1c1f4751140aa\",\"cmd-c8cc1059880b47d2\"],\"summary\":\"bridge vlan show confirms eth1 PVID/Egress Untagged VLAN10, eth2 PVID/Egress Untagged VLAN20, VLAN1 removed\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 (VLAN10) has a working link to node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-97e1c1f4751140aa\"],\"summary\":\"3/3 ping success node1 (192.168.10.1) to node2 (192.168.10.2)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 (VLAN20) has a working link to node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-bfdf7b4704ca4954\"],\"summary\":\"3/3 ping success node1 (192.168.20.1) to node3 (192.168.20.2)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 are isolated from each other despite VLAN separation\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ebc776eca1ed4e40\",\"cmd-38c67fb2aa834741\"],\"summary\":\"node3 given overlapping IP 192.168.10.3/24 on enp8s0; node2 (192.168.10.2) ping to it fails 100% (Destination Host Unreachable), proving VLAN-level L2 isolation rather than mere subnet mismatch\"},{\"requirement\":\"Configuration persists across reboot (systemd unit + NM profiles)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-efa4d935aca041ca\",\"cmd-7f08b237f95f40d3\",\"cmd-8975184b3704448f\",\"cmd-9c8d2601ab364208\"],\"summary\":\"systemd oneshot vlan-access-segmentation.service enabled and idempotent re-run verified on node1; NetworkManager connection profiles enp8s0-vlan10/enp8s0-vlan20 created with autoconnect on node2/node3\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b3052b6d70b048c6\",\"cmd-2f79e54e3e994ff9\",\"cmd-9e5579adb6024300\",\"cmd-997ad1d444d3485f\",\"cmd-9fd4ba7c5ecd4e71\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 67c52137...; reboot acknowledged; new boot_id b55d8d35... confirms restart; VLAN10 IP and NM profile recovered, node1 ping to node2 succeeds post-restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-29ba725786f140aa\",\"cmd-b71b6d3402764f2c\",\"cmd-af4d0f0649ab4ac6\",\"cmd-ae7c2a23d9c0449c\",\"cmd-ff783de3be9a4a04\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 910dc564...; reboot acknowledged; new boot_id 86d074bd... confirms restart; VLAN20 IP and NM profile recovered, node1 ping to node3 succeeds post-restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 (SONiC control-plane) restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state and cluster/service health\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8b885c45dedc49f3\",\"cmd-0b5354bb1c5c4a38\",\"cmd-561996f218ca475e\",\"cmd-8fdc58569a7643e0\",\"cmd-8dec2d294ed24a55\",\"cmd-acbfa004624a4db8\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 39fdb9ab...; reboot acknowledged; new boot_id 7f0b6df0... confirms restart; vlan-access-segmentation.service auto-ran and restored bridge/VLAN/SVI state; docker containers (swss/bgp/syncd/database/gbsyncd) healthy post-restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart re-verification of connectivity and isolation on the fully recovered cluster\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f4fe544a473d404a\",\"cmd-2f79ab8ef1374eb2\",\"cmd-17a0343eafc449b7\",\"cmd-5234947298c447f2\"],\"summary\":\"After all three restarts, node1 pings both node2 and node3 successfully in their respective VLANs, and the overlapping-subnet isolation test between node2/node3 still fails as expected, confirming the segmentation survived the full restart cycle\"}]}","structu